cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Where Does Safety Live? Tracing a Refusal Direction from Base Model to DPO"
abstract: >-
  An investigation of whether Direct Preference Optimization gives a language
  model genuinely richer internal representations of safety, or mainly amplifies
  a pre-existing low-dimensional refusal mechanism. Traces a refusal direction
  across a Base to SFT-Helpful to SFT-Safety to DPO training chain, with a
  parallel branch that varies only the instruction-tuning corpus.
type: software
